  "body": "Old safari would allow large ports, and URL.port of urls like nonspecial://host:65537/ would be capped at 65535, but toString would return the initial given string. I admit this was strange, but changing it found somebody who was relying on our strange behavior, as all URL changes do. I'm curious to know other browsers' views on large ports of custom schemes.",
